      "id": 126892,
      "name": "Oaktree",
      "username": "Oaktree",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/oaktree/{size}/2287_2.png",
      "created_at": "2015-01-12T02:40:37.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"BenjaminTodd\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/b/ecc23a/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> BenjaminTodd:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Deadline's Pandemonium Key reads:</p>\n<blockquote>The first time an environment target enters play each turn, play the top card of the villian deck.\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote>\ndoes this apply when any given envirnomental target enters play or any given type of environmental target?&nbsp; For instance, if The Final Wasteland, if an Amphibious Chupacabra is turned over in two different turns, is that considered one or two targets and therefor two villian card plays?&nbsp;The \"The first time\" phrasing is confusing me, but I read it as each one would trigger the villian card play.Thanks,Ben\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Usually that wording means that if circumstances in that turn trigger the environment playing another card that happens to be a target - you do not trigger the effect again.</p>\n<p>And if the Amphibs came out during different turns it would mean that two villain cards would be played.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
